--- body ---
## Context

Three of four external reviewers (2026-07-27 panel) found the citation-network
description internally ambiguous. The corpus is advertised for citation
network analysis, so this is load-bearing.

**The scale claim.** §2.3 reports 1,087,209 corpus-internal citation pairs
"covering 80% of corpus DOIs". §4 says Figure 2 maps 13,112 connected works.
Figure 2 is captioned at "full-corpus scale". 13,112 is 39% of the 33,344
refined works and 52% of the 25,411 DOI-bearing ones. A reader cannot
reconcile 80% with 39% because the paper never says what the 80% is a share
*of*: DOI-bearing works appearing as citing sources, as cited targets, as
either, or corpus DOIs appearing anywhere in the pair table.

**The no-DOI question.** §3 says works without DOIs cannot be matched as
citing sources, but the same paragraph says GROBID parses unresolved
reference strings and fuzzy-matches them against corpus works. The
`citations.csv` schema has only `source_doi` and `ref_doi`. So does a
title-resolved no-DOI corpus work enter the graph as a *target*? If not — and
the schema says not — the graph systematically excludes no-DOI grey
literature and older works in both directions, not just as citing sources.
24% of the corpus has no DOI. The paper should say this plainly.

**Verification circularity.** The 300-link Crossref check (97.0%, CI
[94.4, 98.4]) is a fine spot check, but many links *originate* from
Crossref/OpenAlex deposits, so verifying them against Crossref is partly
circular. Conversely the nine unconfirmed links may be correct and merely
absent from Crossref. The paper should say what the ground truth is and how
the 300 were stratified. It also validates only link *precision*, never
*recall* — missing links are arguably the more consequential error for
community detection.

**Reproducibility.** Abstracts are not deposited, yet embeddings, semantic
outlier detection, and cross-encoder scores all depend on them. Users can
re-fetch from OpenAlex, but the paper itself notes live indexes drift. So the
central semantic products are not exactly reproducible from the deposit
alone. Two reviewers raised this; it needs one honest sentence, not a fix.

## Relevant files

- `deliverables/data-paper/data-paper.qmd` — §2.3, §3, §4, Figure 2 caption
- `scripts/analysis/compute_citation_coverage.py` — the periodised metric (0317)
- `scripts/analysis/compute_citation_verification.py` — the 300-link check (0320)
- `data/catalogs/refined_citations.csv` — the pair table and its schema
- `deliverables/data-paper/data-paper-vars.yml` — coverage and verification vars

## Actions

1. Define the 80% figure precisely, as a var with a named denominator, and
   state it in the same sentence as 13,112 so the two are reconcilable.
2. Rename Figure 2's caption: it maps the DOI-linked connected subgraph, not
   the full corpus. State the connected-component share on the figure.
3. Answer the no-DOI-target question in §3 in one sentence, from the schema —
   whichever way it goes, say which.
4. State that the Crossref check measures link precision only, that its
   sample was drawn as follows (fill in), and that recall is unmeasured. If
   the sample was unstratified, say so.
5. Add the abstracts-not-deposited reproducibility caveat to §3, naming which
   products (embeddings, outlier flags, relevance scores) are affected.
6. Optional, cheap, asked by two reviewers: a table of the 10 Louvain
   communities — size, top terms, one representative highly-cited work. It
   replaces reader guesswork about an unreadable force-directed layout, and
   it is generated, not written.

## Test

- Red first: a guard asserting the connected-works count and the DOI-coverage
  percentage in the prose are macros sharing a stated denominator var.
- A guard forbidding the string "full-corpus" in Figure 2's caption.
- A guard asserting §3 mentions the abstract-deposit limitation.

## Verification

- [ ] 80% and 13,112 reconcile in the text
- [ ] Figure 2's caption describes the subgraph it actually shows
- [ ] No-DOI works' status as citation targets is stated
- [ ] Precision-only nature of the Crossref check is stated

## Invariants

- Coverage numbers stay generated by `compute_citation_coverage.py`; the
  denominators it emits are the ones the prose must use (0317's lesson —
  the apparent gradient inversion was a denominator artifact).
- If 0332 cuts §4, the Figure 2 caption fix still applies wherever the
  figure lands.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Every citation-network quantity in the paper has a stated denominator
- [ ] The graph's systematic exclusions are disclosed, not implied
